WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:00.875
- [Tyrese Maxey:] In the eighth grade, I told him (Uncle)

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:02.669
I was gonna be a McDonald's All-American.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.838
I told him I was gonna, you know, go to Kentucky

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.132
and try to go to the NBA.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.049
- [Commentator:] Nice screen from Richards.

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:10.635
Maxey in traffic, gets it to go.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:12.012
What a shot from Maxey.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.931
And Tyrese Maxey, first
bucket of the game.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:16.016
He does it with a left.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.351
Maxey, that gets the Wildcats
crowd off their feet.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:32.282
- [Maxey:] So, my alarm
clock goes off at 4:50

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:33.616
every single morning.

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:35.368
Most of the time, my uncle
throws something together,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.411
a little breakfast sandwich,

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:39.497
and then we're getting to
the gym by 5:45. Stretch,

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:41.624
start working out at 6.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:45.128
As soon as the workout is
done at around 7:15, 7:20,

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.379
head to the weight room.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.213
Morning.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.590
- [Receptionist:] Good morning.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.799
- [Maxey:] How are you?

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:50.884
Go get a good lift in

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.428
at about 8 o'clock over
there at Sports Rehab.

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.305
Finish the lift around 9 o'clock.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:56.598
Now I'm coming back at 10;

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:57.724
it's my third workout of the day,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.392
and people haven't even got woken up yet.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.269
That's just a psychological advantage

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:02.937
that I think I have over some players.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:06.274
- [Chris Johnson:] Now you're looking to get
your drag action for three.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:07.609
OK, ready to come get it?

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:12.614
Normally the predraft process
is a little bit faster.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.407
It's about two months.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.326
So, whenever you take a timeframe

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:18.703
like we've experienced in the pandemic,

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:20.914
it has allowed for the people

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.374
that really wanted to put in the time

00:01:23.374 --> 00:01:24.876
to get better.

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:25.710
- You know, it's been different

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.837
because of COVID, for
sure. It's not what I expected,

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:30.507
not what I envisioned in my mind.

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:31.758
But, I mean, it happens.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.176
You know, you have to adapt to the situation.

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:35.053
I like to keep my head down and grind.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:37.222
So, I've got to focus extremely hard

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:38.848
on my grind and just working out

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:41.309
and spending extra time
with family and friends.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:45.396
- [Brandon McKay:] It's just been embracing the
situation, circumstances,

00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:46.356
just been grinding.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:48.274
It's honestly kind of worked out

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.819
cuz it's helped him
just stay in the gym more.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.153
And that's it.

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:54.989
I mean, that's pretty much all he
wants to do anyway is work out.

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:57.200
- When we first got out here,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.036
my entire family was out
here: my mom, my dad,

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:03.081
my sisters, grandmother.

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.583
And we were all out here together.

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.418
But now it's just me and
him, so that's crazy.

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:08.711
That's how you can tell
how long we've been here.

00:02:08.711 --> 00:02:11.589
We got here before summer started,

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:15.009
and we still here when
we in a whole new season.

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:15.844
We in fall now.

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:18.721
So, like, it's just crazy. But, I mean,
it's been cool, man.

00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:20.849
Just been keeping my head low, grinding.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:24.060
Starting at 6 every single
morning, you know, since May 23.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:33.319
- [Johnson:] So, our goal every day for Tyrese
is to make over 2,000 shots.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.072
So if you look at 2,000 times six,

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:38.408
that's what, 12,000 shots a week?

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:42.078
Over a five-, six-month
period, that's a lot of shots.

00:02:42.078 --> 00:02:43.496
And that's made shots.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.499
So it wasn't complex; it was super simple.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.668
This is what we have to correct.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.669
Let's put in the work.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.504
- [Maxey:] It's been great working out with Chris.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.673
I really appreciate him because

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.841
when I first got out here,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.801
they set my schedule for 10 o'clock.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.178
And I told him, I was like—

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.180
he calls the gym the barbershop—

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.973
and I told him I wanted to
be the first one in the shop,

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:04.976
first one in the chair every
single day until I'm gone.

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:07.395
And he said, "OK, fine,
we're gonna get here at 6."

00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:11.608
- [Johnson:] 5:45, 5 a.m. is not for everybody.

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:14.235
Not only basketball players but people

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:17.989
are products of what we do every day,

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.532
like daily routine.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.575
It's like brushing your teeth.

00:03:20.575 --> 00:03:22.118
It's like tying your shoes.

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:23.453
You don't think about it.

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.538
You just do it over and over again.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.290
And that's what basketball is.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.834
It's about creating a routine

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.961
that you can continue to build on top of.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.925
[Crowd cheering]
- [Maxey:] Ahh!

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.968
- [McKay:] Tyrese, he gets the waking up early

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.429
from my mom and his other grandmom.

00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:45.141
They wake up 5:15, 5:30 every morning.

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:47.644
From working out two or three times a day,

00:03:47.644 --> 00:03:51.064
watching film with his dad after games,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.440
watching just regular games,

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.025
whether it's NBA or college,

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:57.278
it just seems like it's
basketball, basketball, basketball.

00:03:57.278 --> 00:03:59.572
- [Maxey:] So in second grade, my dad,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.407
he asked me who my favorite player was.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.034
And I told him Dwyane Wade.

00:04:03.034 --> 00:04:04.744
And his response to that was:

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.454
"If you want to be like Dwyane Wade,

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:08.498
you have to put time in in the gym.

00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:10.250
It's not all about when you go to practice

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.459
and when you play in the game.

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:12.835
You gotta put in after hours.

00:04:12.835 --> 00:04:14.420
You gotta put in extra hours of work.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.006
And outwork people."

00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:19.592
And ever since that day, you know, it
kind of clicked in my mind,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.886
like: "OK, fine. If that's
what it takes to be great,

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:23.012
then that's what I'm gonna do."

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.639
I don't want to have any what-ifs

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:27.100
or "Dang, I wish I could have."

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.352
I wanna be able to say I
laid it all out on the line

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:30.812
and I maximized my potential

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:32.522
and got 1 percent better every single day.

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:34.649
- [Commentator 1:] Maxey the
other way with a spin move. Hangs...and hits!

00:04:34.649 --> 00:04:37.986
- [Commentator 2:] Oh, oh! He is acrobatic. Oh, they love it.

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:41.406
- [Johnson:] You know, there's a major difference

00:04:41.406 --> 00:04:45.326
between being a really elite pro

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:47.912
and being a collegiate basketball player.

00:04:47.912 --> 00:04:50.748
And that separation is in the brain.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:53.543
So when you watch these
great players play,

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:57.171
they can dominate the game
from a mental standpoint.

00:04:57.171 --> 00:04:59.966
They're that much better than
you because of the brain.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.634
And we call it planning from the neck up.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.304
- [Maxey:] My thing is, if you put the work in,

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:07.181
like, I put so much time in in the
gym—these 6 a.m. workouts,

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:11.811
these after-practice shooting
and before-game shooting—

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.396
I have so much confidence in myself.

00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:16.441
So every time I step on the
court, you know, I know what I can do.

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.651
And people ask me, you know, if I made certain shots,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.777
like, "Did you know you can make those?"

00:05:19.777 --> 00:05:22.113
I'm like: "Man, I work on
those shots every single day.

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:22.989
It wasn't nothing new to me."

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.408
- [Commentator 1:] Maxey knocks one down.

00:05:26.242 --> 00:05:27.952
What a big answer.

00:05:27.952 --> 00:05:29.787
- [Commentator 2:] A huge answer by Tyrese Maxey.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:32.373
- [John Calipari:] Tyrese is a winning player.

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:35.168
First of all, he's a
terrific basketball player.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:40.173
And kind of like I've said
about Jamal and Tyler and Shai,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.886
you're gonna regret not taking this kid.

00:05:44.886 --> 00:05:47.597
He falls in the same mode of,

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:51.434
he has all kind of ways
to score the basketball.

00:05:52.727 --> 00:05:55.229
I mean, those kind of kids have
that spirit about 'em.

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:59.400
So, I have a lot of faith in wherever he goes,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.528
they will call me and
say, "Wow, we are so happy

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.322
that we took him."

00:06:04.322 --> 00:06:05.156
- What up?

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:07.283
- [Denyse Maxey:] I was just thinking of you.

00:06:07.283 --> 00:06:09.160
- You're on the camera, so don't be...

00:06:09.994 --> 00:06:11.579
- [Brandon:] Talking crazy.
- Don't be out here talking crazy now.

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:14.290
[Denyse laughing]

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.960
No, you know, you liable to say anything.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.254
- [Denyse:] No, not at all.
How are you today, son?

00:06:20.254 --> 00:06:22.507
- Mm-mm.
[Denyse laughing]

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:25.051
That ain't real. That was fake.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.386
- [Denyse:] Yes, we're super excited.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.303
I can't wait.

00:06:28.429 --> 00:06:29.889
I don't know, I'm excited.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.933
I guess excited and nervous

00:06:31.933 --> 00:06:34.977
and happy and elated all in one emotion.

00:06:34.977 --> 00:06:37.146
That's the scary part, right?

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:39.315
You know, what's gonna happen?

00:06:39.315 --> 00:06:40.733
What number is he gonna go?

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.609
Where is he gonna go?

00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:42.860
Where is he gonna live?

00:06:43.778 --> 00:06:44.821
What is he gonna feel like?

00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:49.200
All of that, all in one emotion, I think.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.494
I guess same thing every
parent feels, right?

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:53.413
- Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.081
- [Johnson:] I can't speak for everyone else

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.333
on the amount of work that was put in.

00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:59.544
But he's not only ready to be drafted,

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:01.087
he's ready to contribute.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:04.257
So, I'm very interested in looking

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:07.385
at what the draft class
looks like this year for him.

00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:08.469
No summer league.

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.556
You know, this is gonna be a new
season for everybody.

00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:13.099
- [McKay:] Every kid has that goal

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:14.851
of becoming a professional athlete.

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:16.394
But to actually know somebody

00:07:16.394 --> 00:07:19.313
or to be related to somebody,
to be close to somebody,

00:07:19.313 --> 00:07:22.066
and you actually see the
whole process play out,

00:07:22.066 --> 00:07:25.736
it's gonna be crazy, and it's
just gonna be a great time.

00:07:25.736 --> 00:07:28.531
- [Maxey:] Not many people can
say that they did exactly

00:07:28.531 --> 00:07:30.116
what they wanted to do with their life.

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.868
So, you know, I was blessed,

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:34.078
and the Lord blessed me to
be able to play basketball.

00:07:34.078 --> 00:07:35.538
I really appreciate Chris.

00:07:35.538 --> 00:07:38.082
And it's just amazing to
have people in your corner.

00:07:38.082 --> 00:07:41.127
Not just him. My dad's been here, my mom,

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.129
my sister, my grandmother,

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:45.256
my nieces. Everybody's been here.

00:07:45.256 --> 00:07:46.132
You know, they all support me.

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:49.010
It's just been an amazing time, and
I can't wait for the future.

